  {
   "title": "The surplus",
   "narration": "Chapter one. The surplus.",
   "beats": [
    {
     "say": "Okay, a small question first. Why would anyone build a village right next to a river that floods every year?",
     "do": [
      {
       "op": "panel",
       "title": "Why by the river?",
       "on": "start"
      },
      {
       "op": "fact",
       "text": "The river floods every year",
       "on": "floods every year"
      }
     ],
     "paragraph": true
    },
    {
     "say": "See, when the water goes back, it leaves soft, rich soil behind.",
     "do": [
      {
       "op": "picture",
       "generate": "a river bank after a flood, dark wet silt, early farmers' fields, warm painted illustration",
       "labels": [
        {
         "name": "river",
         "on": "water"
        },
        {
         "name": "soil",
         "on": "soil"
        },
        {
         "name": "fields",
         "on": "rich soil"
        }
       ],
       "on": "leaves soft, rich soil"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "The fields gave more grain than a family could eat, and the extra went into the granary.",
     "do": [
      {
       "op": "diagram",
       "id": "chain",
       "kind": "flow",
       "title": "Where the grain went",
       "nodes": [
        {
         "id": "fields",
         "label": "Fields"
        },
        {
         "id": "granary",
         "label": "Granary",
         "on": "granary"
        },
        {
         "id": "crafts",
         "label": "Craftsmen"
        },
        {
         "id": "trade",
         "label": "Traders"
        }
       ],
       "show": [
        "fields",
        "granary"
       ],
       "on": "The fields"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "That extra grain is called a surplus.",
     "do": [
      {
       "op": "define",
       "term": "Surplus",
       "meaning": "more than a family needs to eat",
       "on": "surplus"
      }
     ],
     "paragraph": true
    },
    {
     "say": "Now one small thing. With a surplus, not everybody had to farm.",
     "do": [
      {
       "op": "reveal",
       "diagram": "chain",
       "nodes": [
        "crafts"
       ],
       "on": "not everybody had to farm"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Craftsmen made pots and beads, and traders carried them to faraway places.",
